{
  "id": "80507",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Comparing Q and K",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A reversible reaction will always shift toward equilibrium until equilibrium is achieved. By comparing "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Q"
              },
              {
                "text": " and "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": ", we can determine whether a system is at equilibrium—and if it is not, we can determine direction in which it will shift to reach equilibrium."
              }
            ],
            "id": "y7kje2c5bqppph0",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Let's revisit the reaction between hydrogen and iodine to produce hydrogen iodide."
              }
            ],
            "id": "k11rfowxyj9os7f",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "dkl781kmkf6zfjq",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "40djj9r7h2hxxlk",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "{\\mathrm H}_2(g)\\;+\\;{\\mathrm I}_2(g)\\;\\;\\rightleftharpoons\\;\\;2\\;\\mathrm{HI}(g)",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Consider the example we used on the page "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The Reaction Quotient"
                  }
                ],
                "href": "/course/link/iz1ln_the_reaction_quotient_xrgkx",
                "idref": "80784",
                "target": "self",
                "type": "a"
              },
              {
                "text": ", where "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Q"
              },
              {
                "text": " was calculated throughout the progress of the reaction starting with only reactants, H"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " and I"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and no products, HI. We determined that when "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Q"
              },
              {
                "text": " was equal to 9.0, equilibrium had been established because the concentrations of reactants and products stopped changing. For any point in the reaction where "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Q"
              },
              {
                "text": " < "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": ", the ratio "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\frac{\\left[\\mathrm{products}\\right]}{\\left[\\mathrm{reactants}\\right]}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " is smaller than the equilibrium value, so the reaction will proceed toward equilibrium by shifting to the right."
              }
            ],
            "id": "mhpmr0k88l9cc74",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Starting with only H"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " and I"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": ", the reaction forms HI and proceeds to the right until equilibrium is reached. The arrows represent the relative rates of the forward and reverse reactions at each point."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "pidbyhkfnbwfqb2",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "bqoscbudyzlbnxc",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/39/39bde36162a78156d5786373c0c007e7/q_less_than_k.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "700"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Now let's look at the same reaction, under the same conditions, but this time we begin the reaction with all products, HI, and no reactants. As previously discussed, the value for "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": " will be the same regardless of the concentrations of reactants and products you begin with. Because the temperature has not changed, "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": " is still equal to 9. For any point in the reaction where "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "Q"
              },
              {
                "text": " > "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "K"
              },
              {
                "text": ", the ratio "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\frac{\\left[\\mathrm{products}\\right]}{\\left[\\mathrm{reactants}\\right]}",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " is larger than the equilibrium value, so the reaction will proceed toward equilibrium by shifting to the left."
              }
            ],
            "id": "ljjc3js6jci4dct",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "Starting with only HI, the reaction forms H"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " and I"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "sub": true,
                    "text": "2"
                  },
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": " and proceeds to the left until equilibrium is reached. The arrows represent the relative rates of the forward and reverse reactions at each point."
                  }
                ],
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "l31li16msn5o2ow",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "0ga8qzmkl1wb1v8",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/b7/b71a49a3870648149b96b9075dbb9dd4/q_greater_than_k.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "700"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "4089747868",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
        "id": "568359569",
